          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %em Koszul complex
            of a sequence of elements
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x_1, \cdots, x_d)
            in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+ring"} commutative ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            (or more generally of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/center"} central
            elements in a
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-commutative+ring"} non-commutative ring
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cochain+complex"} cochain complex
            whose entry in degree
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} -n
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exterior+power"} exterior power
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mo ∧
                    %mi n
                  %msup
                    %mi R
                    %mi d
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \wedge^n R^d
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+module"} free module
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi R
                    %mi d
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi R
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo ⊕
                        %mi d
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R^d = R^{\oplus_d}
            over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rank"} rank
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential"} differential
            is given in each degree on the
            = succeed "th" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_k
          %p
            The key property of the Koszul complex is that in good cases (namely if the sequence
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x_1, \cdots, x_d)
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+sequence"} regular sequence
            in
            = succeed ")," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+resolution"} free
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homological+resolution"} homological resolution
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient"} quotient
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R/(x_1, \cdots, x_d)
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ideal"} ideal
            generated by these elements (see prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#KoszulComplexOfRegularSequenceIsFreeResolutionOfQuotientRing"}
            below).
          %p
            In cases where the Koszul complex fails to be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homological+resolution"} homological resolution
            of the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+ring"} quotient ring
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Koszul-Tate+resolution"} Koszul-Tate resolution
          %p
            From the perspective of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+algebraic+geometry"} derived algebraic geometry
            the Koszul complex may be interpreted as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+duality"} formal dual
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+critical+locus"} derived critical locus
            of the elements
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x_1, \cdots, x_d)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum+of+a+ring"} spectrum
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Spec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec(R)
          %p
            In this guise the Koszul complex appears prominently in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+field+theory"} Lagrangian field theory
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BV-complex"} BV-complex
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homological+resolution"} homological resolution
            of the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shell"} shell
            (the solution locus of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euler-Lagrange+equations"} Euler-Lagrange
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equations+of+motion"} equations of motion
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#KoszulResolutionForNoetherianRngAndElementsInJacobson"}
            below) which has the interpretation as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+gauge+symmetries"} infinitesimal gauge symmetries
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+density"} Lagrangian density
            that have not been made explicit. Making them explicit by promoting them to elements in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chevalley-Eilenberg+algebra"} Chevalley-Eilenberg algebra
            of the corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+Lie+algebroid"} action Lie algebroid
            yields what is called the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BRST+complex"} BRST complex
            of the theory, and
            %em its
            Koszul complex then yields the respective
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Koszul-Tate+resolution"} Koszul-Tate resolution
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BV-BRST+complex"} BV-BRST complex
            of the theory.
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            be a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unital+ring"} unital ring
          %p
            Consider also a finite
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sequence"} sequence
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mi r
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x_1,\ldots,x_r)
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elements"} elements
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mi i
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_i \in R
          %p
            Given any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/center"} central element
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\in Z(R)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cochain+complex"} cochain complex
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %mo →
                  %mi R
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi x
                  %mi R
                  %mo →
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(x) \coloneqq (0\to R\stackrel{x}\to R\to 0)
          %p
            concentrated in degrees
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential"} differential
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mi r
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x_1,\ldots,x_r)
            of central elements in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            one can define the tensor product
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mi r
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi R
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi R
                  %mi ⋯
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi R
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mi r
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  K(x_1,\ldots,x_r)
                  \\coloneqq
                  K(x_1)\otimes_R K(x_2)\otimes_R\cdots \otimes_R K(x_r)
          %p
            of complexes of left
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modules"} modules
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            part of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 1
